@startuml
' TUTORIAL 4 - Activity 4.
'
' The three rules task 16 asks you to check:
'   (a) the hollow triangle touches Product, not the children
'   (b) neither child box repeats id, name or price
'   (c) fields are marked -, methods are marked +
class Product {
  - id : Long
  - name : String
  - price : double
  + getName() : String
  + getPrice() : double
}
class DigitalProduct {
  ' TWO fields only. The three inherited ones are NOT repeated -
  ' the arrow already says this class has them. Repeating them
  ' claims the child declares its own separate copies, which would
  ' be a different (and wrong) design.
  - downloadUrl : String
  - fileSizeMB : double
  + getDownloadUrl() : String
}
class PhysicalProduct {
  - weightKg : double
  - dimensions : String
  + getWeightKg() : double
}
' ===== The inheritance arrows =====
' <|-- is GENERALISATION (extends): a SOLID line with a HOLLOW
' TRIANGLE at the parent end.
'
' In PlantUML the PARENT goes on the LEFT. Read "Product <|--
' DigitalProduct" as "Product is generalised by DigitalProduct", or
' more usefully: the triangle ends up touching Product.
'
' Draw it the other way round and the diagram claims Product extends
' DigitalProduct - the opposite of your code. The guide calls this
' "the single most frequent mistake in submitted diagrams", so look
' at the RENDERED picture, not just this text.
Product <|-- DigitalProduct
Product <|-- PhysicalProduct
' Coming in Tutorial 5: a second arrow type, <|.. with DOTS, for
' implements. One character apart from this one, and markers check it.
@enduml